---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import KnowledgeLoop from '../components/KnowledgeLoop.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { TOPICS } from '../data/taxonomy';

const trajectory = [
  { stage: 'Independent investigation', now: true },
  { stage: 'Accumulated findings' },
  { stage: 'A tested research method' },
  { stage: 'Experiments and tools' },
  { stage: 'Collaboration' },
  { stage: 'Multidisciplinary research' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Why FalconProSec exists, what it investigates, how it works, and where it is heading: an independent research initiative on technology, cybersecurity, AI and human behavior."
>
  <PageHeader
    kicker="About"
    title="Technology is changing how people trust, decide and protect themselves."
    description={`${SITE.name} is an independent research initiative investigating problems at the intersection of technology, cybersecurity, AI and human behavior, with the people affected at the center.`}
  />

  <div class="container-site mt-16 space-y-20">
    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="why">
      <h2 id="why" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        Why it exists
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          FalconProSec exists to understand how technological progress changes 
          the way people live, make decisions, trust one another, and experience risk. An
          automated decision is a piece of software and a
          consequence in someone's life. Understanding these problems takes
          more than one discipline, and often the right one is not obvious at
          the start.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="what">
      <h2 id="what" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        What it does
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          {SITE.name} investigates specific questions where technology,
          cybersecurity, AI, human behavior, trust and safety meet. Each
          investigation asks who is affected, how, and why the technology makes
          it possible, and ends with what remains unknown.
        </p>
        <p>
          The aim is not to publish for the sake of publishing. Each
          investigation should add to a body of knowledge: findings that hold
          up across cases, patterns that recur, and better questions for the
          next investigation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]">
        <h2 id="how" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
          How it works
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <p>
            Investigations follow evidence, examine technical and human
            factors together, and document findings separately from
            interpretation. Where it helps, something is built or tested to
            see whether an explanation holds.
          </p>
          <a href="/methods" class="link inline-block text-base">Read the full method</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <KnowledgeLoop />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="areas">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]">
        <h2 id="areas" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
          Areas of inquiry
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The work is organised around problems, not specialties. These five
          areas overlap, and they are expected to change as investigations
          reveal connections between them.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          TOPICS.map((t) => (
            <li class="bg-ink p-6">
              <a href={`/topics/${t.slug}`} class="font-heading font-semibold text-white hover:text-primary-text">
                {t.label}
              </a>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{t.inquiry}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
        <li class="bg-ink p-6">
          <a href="/research" class="font-heading font-semibold text-primary-text hover:text-white">
            The research agenda →
          </a>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
            The specific questions currently being explored in each area.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="today">
      <h2 id="today" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        Where it stands today
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          {SITE.name} is at an early stage. It is an independent initiative
          run by one person, with no institutional affiliation, no team, and
          no clients. It does not offer professional security services.
        </p>
        <p>
          Its credibility has to come from the work itself: the quality of the
          questions, the care taken with evidence, and whether the
          investigations build on each other over time. Where something has not
          yet been demonstrated, the site says so.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="direction">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]">
        <h2 id="direction" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
          What it may become
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <p>
            The long-term direction is a multidisciplinary research
            organisation, where people from cybersecurity, engineering, AI,
            psychology, behavioral science and other fields work together on
            problems none of them could fully understand alone.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is a direction, not a claim. If it happens, it should grow out
            of the research: findings that justify a method, a method that
            invites collaboration, collaboration that needs structure.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase" aria-label="Path of development">
        {
          trajectory.map((t, i) => (
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
              {i > 0 && <span class="text-subtle" aria-hidden="true">→</span>}
              <span
                class:list={[
                  'rounded-full border px-3 py-1.5',
                  t.now
                    ? 'border-primary bg-primary/15 text-white'
                    : 'border-line text-subtle',
                ]}
              >
                {t.stage}
                {t.now && <span class="ml-2 text-primary-text">· Now</span>}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="who">
      <h2 id="who" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        Who is behind it
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          Hello! I'm Sandra. My background is in computer science, so I
          understand technology from the side of the people who build it: the
          decisions, the trade-offs, and the shortcuts that seem harmless at
          the time.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started {SITE.name} because I kept arriving at questions about what
          happens when that technology reaches people, and those questions did
          not belong to any single field. I'm not claiming expertise in every
          discipline the work touches. I'm following the problems, learning
          what they require, and showing the work as it develops.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="corrections">
      <h2 id="corrections" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        Corrections
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          When an error is found in an investigation or finding, it is
          corrected on the page and noted in a visible “Corrections & updates”
          section with the date, rather than changed silently.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you notice something wrong or have more context,
          <a href="/contact?reason=correction" class="link">please get in touch</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <CTASection
      title="Start with a question"
      description="Read the current investigations, or suggest a question about technology and people that deserves a closer look."
      primary={{ href: '/investigations', label: 'Explore Investigations' }}
      secondary={{ href: '/contact?reason=investigation', label: 'Suggest a question' }}
    />
  </div>
</Layout>
